1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,366
A slider-crank turns
spinning motion into

2
00:00:03,366 --> 00:00:07,266
back-and-forth motion, as
in an engine or a pump.

3
00:00:07,866 --> 00:00:13,000
Input: the crank turns. Its pin
travels in a circle of radius 18 mm.

4
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:19,866
The connecting rod (62 mm) links the crank
pin to the piston and pushes and pulls it.

5
00:00:20,466 --> 00:00:24,133
The piston slides along a
straight line. Its stroke

6
00:00:24,133 --> 00:00:27,333
is twice the crank
radius: 36 mm per turn.
